  <name>Canto</name>
  <developer id="io.github.gusthanks">
     <name>Gustavo Costa</name>
  </developer>
  <summary>Spotify client with synced lyrics</summary>

  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#c7f8d3</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#354762</color>
  </branding>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.gusthanks.Canto.desktop</launchable>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>

  <content_rating type="oars-1.1" />

  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">360</display_length>
  </requires>

  <recommends>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>pointing</control>
    <control>touch</control>
  </recommends>

  <description>
    <p>Canto is a Spotify client for the Linux desktop that puts your library, synced lyrics and listening flow front and center, without visual clutter.</p>
    <p><em>Note: Canto requires a Spotify Premium account.</em></p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Synced lyrics in the side panel or full screen, with the active line lighting up word by word</li>
      <li>Colors that follow your desktop theme (including Omarchy themes, live) or the album cover</li>
      <li>Now Playing panel with a big cover, lyrics preview, the next track and song credits</li>
      <li>Your Library as a list or a grid of covers, with pinned items and a collapsed covers-only sidebar</li>
      <li>Reopens on the track you closed it on, right where it stopped</li>
      <li>Play here or on any Spotify Connect device, such as phones and smart speakers</li>
      <li>Command palette (Ctrl+K) for navigation, themes, devices, sleep timer and search</li>
      <li>Track radio, sleep timer, and scrobbling to Last.fm and ListenBrainz</li>
      <li>Gapless playback with a 10-band equalizer, stereo pan and pitch shift</li>
      <li>Media keys (MPRIS), keyboard shortcuts and touch gestures</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Canto is a fork of Riff by Diego Augusto and contributors, itself descended from Spot by Alexandre Trendel.</p>
  </description>

